<div id="S6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Bootstrapped analyses (Figure <a href="#S6" title="6 Study 3: Human vs. LLM with Personas ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) confirm this pattern across the four conditions. Relative to the default LLM, creative entrepreneurs show significantly higher diversity across all metrics: unique categories (<math id="S6.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{entrepreneur}}=22.98" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>entrepreneur</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>22.98</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{entrepreneur}}=22.98</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.11</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S6.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{default}}=18.45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>default</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>18.45</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{default}}=18.45</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.11</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>), unique combinations (<math id="S6.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{entrepreneur}}=50.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>entrepreneur</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>50.40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{entrepreneur}}=50.40</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.45</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.45</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S6.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{default}}=39.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>default</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>39.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{default}}=39.15</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.32</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>), and average pairwise distance (<math id="S6.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{entrepreneur}}=2.28" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>entrepreneur</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.28</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{entrepreneur}}=2.28</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.01</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S6.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{default}}=2.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>default</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{default}}=2.04</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>). However, creative entrepreneurs still fall short of ordinary personas. Ordinary personas generate more unique categories (<math id="S6.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona}}=24.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>persona</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>24.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona}}=24.02</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.13</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>), more unique combinations (<math id="S6.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=56.97" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>persona</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>56.97</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=56.97</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.51" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.51</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.51</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>), and higher pairwise distances (<math id="S6.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{persona}}=2.36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>persona</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.36</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{persona}}=2.36</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>). Overall, these findings demonstrate that ordinary personas are a particularly effective LLM-based approach for closing the human–LLM idea diversity gap.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S6.fig1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_3_bootsrapped.png" id="S6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/213;" width="476" height="213" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S6.fig1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 3 Bootstrapped Diversity Comparison: Human vs. LLM (Default and Persona).</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S6.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Persona Fixation Analysis. </span>
Despite these aggregate gains, imbuing LLMs with personas is not without risk when it comes to individual-level diversity. As discussed previously, unique mental models play a dual role in human creativity: knowledge partitioning helps collective human diversity, but mental models can undermine within-individual diversity through fixation. Thus, by assigning a specific persona to an LLM, are we unwittingly increasing fixation? Our findings suggest that the answer depends on the type of persona. As Figure <a href="#S6" title="6 Study 3: Human vs. LLM with Personas ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows, ordinary personas increased fixation relative to the default condition: the ordinary persona condition exhibited less steep slopes than the default condition for unique categories (<math id="S6.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{default}}=1.0131" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>default</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0131</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{default}}=1.0131</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{persona}}=0.876" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>persona</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.876</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{persona}}=0.876</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>), indicating greater within-individual fixation. By contrast, creative entrepreneurs did not change fixation relative to the default condition: slopes were statistically indistinguishable from the default condition for unique categories (<math id="S6.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{entrepreneur}}=0.985" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>entrepreneur</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.985</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{entrepreneur}}=0.985</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.40</annotation></semantics></math>). One possible explanation is that ordinary personas provide more concrete, everyday cues that stabilize a participant’s exploratory path, whereas creative entrepreneur cues are broader and less anchoring, leaving within-participant exploration largely unaffected. Therefore, while personas can enhance diversity across participants, some persona types (ordinary personas) may simultaneously reinforce a stable schema that constrains exploration within a participant, whereas others (creative entrepreneurs) do so less.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.fig2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S6.fig2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_3_fixation.png" id="S6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/230;" width="333" height="230" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S6.fig2.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 3 Fixation Analysis: Within-Individual Diversity Accumulation for LLM Default vs. LLM with Persona.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S6.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Knowledge Partitioning (First Ideas). </span>
To examine how personas influence knowledge partitioning, we analyzed the first ideas generated by each participant (Figure <a href="#S6" title="6 Study 3: Human vs. LLM with Personas ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). LLMs prompted with ordinary personas produced initial ideas with higher unique combinations than humans (<math id="S6.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=9.43" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>persona</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>9.43</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=9.43</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.07" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.07</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.07</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S6.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{human}}=9.17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>human</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>9.17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{human}}=9.17</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.09" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.09</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.09</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.02</annotation></semantics></math>) and very similar performance on the other metrics. In comparison, LLM Creative Entrepreneurs showed significantly lower first-idea diversity than humans and ordinary personas in unique categories (<math id="S6.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{entrepreneur}}=12.63" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>entrepreneur</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>12.63</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{entrepreneur}}=12.63</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.18</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S6.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona}}=14.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>persona</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>14.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona}}=14.35</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.17</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>), unique combinations (<math id="S6.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{entrepreneur}}=8.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>entrepreneur</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>8.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{entrepreneur}}=8.50</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.11</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S6.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=9.43" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>persona</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>9.43</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=9.43</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.07" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.07</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.07</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>), and pairwise distance (<math id="S6.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{entrepreneur}}=2.18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>entrepreneur</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{entrepreneur}}=2.18</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.02</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S6.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{persona}}=2.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>persona</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{persona}}=2.35</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.02</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>). These results are suggestive that creative entrepreneur prompts do not occupy as distinct regions of the idea space as ordinary personas, and thus induce less knowledge partitioning.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.fig3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S6.fig3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_3_first_ideas.png" id="S6.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/213;" width="476" height="213" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S6.fig3.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 3 Knowledge Partitioning Based on First Ideas Only for Human vs. LLM with Persona.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S6.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Knowledge Partitioning (Embedding Analysis).</span>
To provide more direct evidence of knowledge partitioning, we conducted an idea-level embedding analysis across the LLM Default, LLM Ordinary Persona, LLM Creative Entrepreneur, and Human conditions. Each session includes all ten ideas generated by an individual – either a human participant or a simulated LLM agent. This methodology allows us to map abstract distributional properties like knowledge partitioning into a measurable semantic space. Each generated idea was vectorized using the OpenAI text-embedding-3-small model, resulting in a 1,536-dimensional representation. For visualization only, we used t-SNE to reduce these embeddings to two dimensions (see Figure <a href="#S6" title="6 Study 3: Human vs. LLM with Personas ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> as an example). All statistical metrics were computed in the original 1,536-dimensional embedding space.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p12.1" class="ltx_p">For a given participant <math id="S6.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> generating <math id="S6.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> ideas represented by vectors <math id="S6.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{s,1},\dots,v_{s,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{s,1},\dots,v_{s,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the participant-level centroid <math id="S6.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> as the mean vector:</p>
<table id="S6.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{p}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}v_{p,i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{p}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}v_{p,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Between-Participant Variation:</span>
Knowledge partitioning determines the neighborhood from which information is retrieved by a participant. We measure partitioning by computing the average pairwise Euclidean distance between the centroids of <math id="S6.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> participants:</p>
<table id="S6.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{between}}=\frac{1}{m(m-1)}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sum_{j\neq i}^{m}\|C_{i}-C_{j}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>between</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{between}}=\frac{1}{m(m-1)}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sum_{j\neq i}^{m}\|C_{i}-C_{j}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p13.2" class="ltx_p">Higher between-participant variation indicates greater separation in the semantic space accessed across participants. We use this as a proxy for knowledge partitioning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p14.1" class="ltx_p">As Figure <a href="#S6" title="6 Study 3: Human vs. LLM with Personas ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows, LLM Ordinary Persona achieves the highest between-participant variation (<math id="S6.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=0.635" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.635</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=0.635</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.045" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.045</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.045</annotation></semantics></math>), which is 2.6 times higher than LLM Default (<math id="S6.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=0.241" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.241</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=0.241</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.014" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.014</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.014</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S6.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>) and exceeding Human (<math id="S6.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=0.545" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.545</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=0.545</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.035" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.035</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.035</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S6.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>). Ordinary Personas also outperform Creative Entrepreneurs (<math id="S6.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=0.429" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.429</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=0.429</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.044" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.044</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.044</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S6.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>). This pattern is visually apparent in Figure <a href="#S6" title="6 Study 3: Human vs. LLM with Personas ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, which plots one bootstrap iteration: the session centroids for LLM Default cluster tightly in the center, whereas Creative Entrepreneur, Ordinary Persona and Human centroids are distributed across distinct regions of the semantic space, with Ordinary Personas exhibiting the greatest dispersion. These findings support our argument that personas recover knowledge partitioning by accessing different idea space regions, with ordinary personas outperforming creative archetypes by carrying more varied cues that push ideas into more distant semantic neighborhoods.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.fig4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S6.fig4.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_3_spread.png" id="S6.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:191/210;" width="191" height="210" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S6.fig4.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 3: Between-Participant Variation.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.fig5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S6.fig5.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_3_partitioning.png" id="S6.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/138;" width="476" height="138" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S6.fig5.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 3: t-SNE visualization of idea embeddings across conditions. 
10 participants per condition. Each dot represents one idea, and each x marks the centroid for that participant.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S6.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p15.1" class="ltx_p">In sum, personas contribute positively in one dimension (partitioning across participants) but can impose costs in another (fixation within an participant), and this trade-off depends on the persona type. To address this potential cost, we turn to Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting, which may counteract fixation by adding an ordered reasoning structure that encourages broader exploration across the solution space. Importantly, CoT may uniquely benefit LLMs rather than humans, reflecting one advantage of LLMs: their ability to follow instructions. Study 4 tests whether CoT can offset any fixation induced by personas and whether the two methods, when combined, produce complementary benefits.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Study 4: Chain-of-Thought Effects on LLM Diversity and Fixation</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Study 3 showed that assigning LLMs ordinary personas enhanced both initial and subsequent idea diversity, boosting overall diversity, but also increasing fixation. Study 4 tests whether Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting could reduce the fixation introduced by ordinary personas, thus optimizing LLM idea diversity. CoT prompting encourages broader exploration by breaking the generation process into a series of structured reasoning steps. Prior research has shown that this approach can enhance the diversity and originality of LLM-generated ideas <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Meincke et al. 2024b</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">De Freitas et al. 2025</a>)</cite>. For example, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">De Freitas et al. (2025)</a></cite> demonstrated that explicitly prompting models to adopt the following multi-step ideation process led to substantial improvements in creative output:</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S7.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="62.62" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 62.62" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,62.62) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 56.71 C 0 59.97 2.64 62.62 5.91 62.62 L 471.47 62.62 C 474.73 62.62 477.38 59.97 477.38 56.71 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 36.97 L 475.41 36.97 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 46.33)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S7.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="S7.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">CoT Prompt from de Freitas et al. (2025)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.38" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S7.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="S7.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx18" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Follow</span><span id="lstnumberx18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">these</span><span id="lstnumberx18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">steps</span><span id="lstnumberx18.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span><span id="lstnumberx18.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Do</span><span id="lstnumberx18.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">each</span><span id="lstnumberx18.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">step</span><span id="lstnumberx18.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,</span><span id="lstnumberx18.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">even</span><span id="lstnumberx18.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">if</span><span id="lstnumberx18.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">you</span><span id="lstnumberx18.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">think</span><span id="lstnumberx18.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">you</span><span id="lstnumberx18.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">do</span><span id="lstnumberx18.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">not</span><span id="lstnumberx18.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">need</span><span id="lstnumberx18.30" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.31" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">to</span><span id="lstnumberx18.32" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx19" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First</span><span id="lstnumberx19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,</span><span id="lstnumberx19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">generate</span><span id="lstnumberx19.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx19.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">a</span><span id="lstnumberx19.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx19.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">list</span><span id="lstnumberx19.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx19.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">of</span><span id="lstnumberx19.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx19.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">30</span><span id="lstnumberx19.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx19.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">ideas</span><span id="lstnumberx19.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-s