<span id="S7.tab1.2.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">248</span>
<span id="S7.tab1.2.1.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">830 <span id="S7.tab1.2.1.7.4.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\down</span></span></span>
</span></p>
</figure>
<div id="S7.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p15.1" class="ltx_p">Bootstrapped analysis (Figure <a href="#S7" title="7 Study 4: Chain-of-Thought Effects on LLM Diversity and Fixation ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) further supports these findings and highlights key differences in how CoT affects LLMs and humans. For LLMs, adding CoT yields statistically significant gains across all three diversity metrics when applied to the default model.
Unique categories increase from <math id="S7.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{default}}=18.45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>default</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>18.45</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{default}}=18.45</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.11</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S7.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{CoT}}=24.84" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>24.84</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{CoT}}=24.84</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.11</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>;
unique combinations rise from <math id="S7.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{default}}=39.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>default</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>39.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{default}}=39.15</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.32</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S7.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{CoT}}=55.49" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>55.49</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{CoT}}=55.49</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.36</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.36</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>;
and pairwise distance increases from <math id="S7.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{default}}=2.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>default</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{default}}=2.04</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S7.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{CoT}}=2.39" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.39</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{CoT}}=2.39</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.00</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>.
When combined with personas, CoT again enhances diversity across all metrics.
Total categories rise from <math id="S7.p15.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona}}=24.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>persona</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>24.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona}}=24.02</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.13</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S7.p15.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona CoT}}=26.51" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>persona CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>26.51</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona CoT}}=26.51</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.08" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.08</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>;
unique combinations from <math id="S7.p15.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=56.97" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>persona</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>56.97</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=56.97</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.51" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.51</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.51</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S7.p15.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona CoT}}=65.42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>persona CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>65.42</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona CoT}}=65.42</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>;
and pairwise distance from <math id="S7.p15.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{persona}}=2.36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>persona</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.36</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{persona}}=2.36</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S7.p15.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{persona CoT}}=2.48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>persona CoT</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.48</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{persona CoT}}=2.48</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p15.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p16.1" class="ltx_p">For humans, however, CoT does not lead to higher diversity.
Unique categories decrease from <math id="S7.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{human}}=26.29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>human</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>26.29</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{human}}=26.29</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.10</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S7.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{human CoT}}=25.36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>human CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>25.36</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{human CoT}}=25.36</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.13</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>;
unique combinations from <math id="S7.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{human}}=59.66" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>human</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>59.66</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{human}}=59.66</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.47" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.47</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.47</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S7.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{human CoT}}=59.81" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>human CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>59.81</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{human CoT}}=59.81</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.43" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.43</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.43</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.814" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.814</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.814</annotation></semantics></math>;
and pairwise distance from <math id="S7.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{human}}=2.41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>human</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.41</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{human}}=2.41</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.00</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S7.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{human CoT}}=2.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>human CoT</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{human CoT}}=2.40</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.00</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.145" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.145</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.145</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.fig2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S7.fig2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_4_bootstrapped.png" id="S7.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/180;" width="476" height="180" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S7.fig2.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 4 Bootstrapped Diversity Comparison: Human vs. LLM (Default and CoT).</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S7.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fixation Analysis. </span>
Study 3 showed that personas increase fixation within individual agents by anchoring idea generation to a stable mental model. Here, we test whether CoT can counteract this effect and reduce fixation, both for default LLMs and for persona-based ones. Fixation is again measured as the slope of diversity accumulation across 10 ideas, where steeper slopes indicate broader, less constrained idea exploration and thus lower fixation. As shown in Figure <a href="#S7" title="7 Study 4: Chain-of-Thought Effects on LLM Diversity and Fixation ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>(a), CoT significantly reduces fixation in LLMs. Compared to the Default condition, CoT yields steeper slopes for unique categories (<math id="S7.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{default}}=1.013" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>default</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.013</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{default}}=1.013</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.017" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.017</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.017</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S7.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{CoT}}=1.363" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.363</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{CoT}}=1.363</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.020" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.020</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.020</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S7.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>), indicating reduced fixation. Adding CoT to personas also decreases fixation relative to using personas alone, producing steeper slopes (categories: <math id="S7.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{persona}}=0.876" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>persona</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.876</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{persona}}=0.876</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.029" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.029</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.029</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S7.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{persona CoT}}=1.086" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>persona CoT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.086</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{persona CoT}}=1.086</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.030" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.030</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.030</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S7.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>). In general, these results suggest that CoT is an effective mechanism for LLMs to reduce individual fixation, both alone and paired with personas.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p18.1" class="ltx_p">For humans, CoT has no meaningful effect on fixation. As shown in Figure <a href="#S7" title="7 Study 4: Chain-of-Thought Effects on LLM Diversity and Fixation ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>(b), the Human and Human CoT conditions yield nearly identical accumulation slopes for categories (<math id="S7.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{human}}=1.035" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>human</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.035</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{human}}=1.035</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.029" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.029</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.029</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S7.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{human CoT}}=1.035" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>human CoT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.035</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{human CoT}}=1.035</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.029" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.029</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.029</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S7.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.997" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.997</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.997</annotation></semantics></math>). This suggests that while CoT offers an external reasoning structure that helps LLMs overcome fixation, humans may not be able to challenge their own fixation in the same way: once a line of thinking is established, it may be cognitively difficult to deviate from it even with explicit structure.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.fig3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S7.fig3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_4_fixation.png" id="S7.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/157;" width="476" height="157" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S7.fig3.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 4 Fixation Analysis: Diversity Accumulation for (a) LLMs With and Without CoT and Personas; and (b) Humans With and Without CoT.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S7.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Knowledge Partitioning (First Ideas).</span>
We have shown above that CoT reduces within-individual fixation. Here, we ask whether CoT also helps recover knowledge partitioning by examining first-idea diversity under different conditions. As shown in Figure <a href="#S7" title="7 Study 4: Chain-of-Thought Effects on LLM Diversity and Fixation ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, CoT leads to a significant improvement over the default LLM across all three metrics, but the effect sizes are small: unique categories increase from <math id="S7.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{default}}=8.37" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>default</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>8.37</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{default}}=8.37</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.11</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{CoT}}=9.23" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>9.23</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{CoT}}=9.23</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.16</annotation></semantics></math>, unique combinations from <math id="S7.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{default}}=5.88" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>default</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>5.88</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{default}}=5.88</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.13</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{CoT}}=6.73" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>6.73</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{CoT}}=6.73</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.12</annotation></semantics></math>, and pairwise distance from <math id="S7.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{default}}=1.51" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>default</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1.51</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{default}}=1.51</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.02</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{CoT}}=1.73" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1.73</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{CoT}}=1.73</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.03</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.03</annotation></semantics></math>, all <math id="S7.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>). This suggests that CoT modestly increases starting-point diversity relative to the default LLM, but does not substantially shift where ideas begin.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.fig4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S7.fig4.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_4_first_ideas.png" id="S7.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/180;" width="476" height="180" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S7.fig4.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 4: First Ideas Only for Different LLM Conditions.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S7.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Knowledge Partitioning (Embedding Analysis).</span>
To further assess whether CoT recovers knowledge partitioning, we ran the same embedding-based analysis as in Study 3, comparing LLM Default, LLM CoT, LLM Ordinary Persona, and Human. As Figure <a href="#S7" title="7 Study 4: Chain-of-Thought Effects on LLM Diversity and Fixation ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows, ordinary personas achieve the highest between-participant variation (<math id="S7.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=0.635" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.635</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=0.635</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.045" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.045</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.045</annotation></semantics></math>), whereas CoT yields only a modest increase over the default condition (<math id="S7.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=0.318" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.318</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=0.318</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.010" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.010</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.010</annotation></semantics></math>). Consistent with this, Figure <a href="#S7" title="7 Study 4: Chain-of-Thought Effects on LLM Diversity and Fixation ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (one bootstrap iteration) shows that session centroids for LLM Default and LLM CoT cluster tightly near the center of the semantic space, while LLM Ordinary Persona and Human centroids are dispersed across distinct regions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.fig5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S7.fig5.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_4_spread.png" id="S7.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:191/210;" width="191" height="210" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S7.fig5.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 4: Between-Participant Variation.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<figure id="S7.fig6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span id="S7.fig6.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\FIGURE</span><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20408v1/study_4_partitioning.png" id="S7.g7" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/138;" width="476" height="138" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S7.fig6.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Study 4: t-SNE visualization of idea embeddings across conditions. 
10 participants per condition. Each dot represents one idea, and each x marks the centroid for that participant.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S7.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Taken together, Study 4 shows that CoT and personas improve idea diversity in LLMs through distinct yet complementary mechanisms. Ordinary personas help recover knowledge partitioning across participants, but this approach increases fixation. CoT, on the other hand, reduces fixation by promoting more flexible sequential reasoning, without meaningfully affecting knowledge partitioning. When combined, these two complementary approaches produce the highest levels of idea diversity across all metrics. For humans, however, CoT neither reduces fixation nor improves idea diversity, indicating that it offers little benefit when applied to human ideation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Summary of Findings</h2>

<figure id="S8.tab1" class="ltx_table"><span id="S8.tab1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\TABLE</span>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<p id="S8.tab1.2" class="ltx_p">Summary of Study Designs and Main Findings
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">


<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.6pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Study</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experiment Design</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Main Findings</span></span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.6pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Study 1: Human vs. Default LLM</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">99 humans vs. 99 default LLMs.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Humans significantly outperformed LLMs in overall idea diversity. Fixation levels were similar, but LLMs showed much lower across-individual diversity, especially in first ideas.</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.6pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Study 2: Human vs. LLM with Human Seeds</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">99 humans vs. 99 seeded LLMs. Each LLM agent was seeded with a human first idea, then generated 9 additional ideas.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Seeding did not improve subsequent LLM idea diversity, suggesting an LLM cannot be reliably moved to a different region of the idea space simply by providing a different starting idea. This implies the limitation lies not only in where ideas begin, but also in how they unfold across subsequent steps.</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.6pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Study 3: Human vs. LLM with Personas</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">99 humans vs. 99 LLMs with ordinary personas vs. 99 LLMs with creative entrepreneurs. Each LLM agent was assigned a unique persona.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Personas significantly boosted diversity relative to default LLMs, improving first-idea diversity and subsequent idea generation and bringing overall diversity close to human levels. Ordinary personas outperformed creative entrepreneurs. Gains came mainly from increased across-individual diversity (recovering knowledge partitioning), but ordinary personas also increased within-individual fixation.</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.6pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Study 4: CoT on Humans and LLMs</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">83 humans vs. 83 humans + CoT; 83 LLM default vs. 83 LLM + CoT; 83 LLM persona vs. 83 LLM persona + CoT.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.65pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab1.2.1.1.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">CoT significantly boosted diversity relative to default LLMs, though less than ordinary personas. Gains came mainly from reduced fixation. When combined with ordinary personas, CoT produced the strongest results, surpassing humans by 26%. For humans, CoT offered no benefits and slightly reduced diversity.</span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></p>
</figure>
<figure id="S8.tab2" class="ltx_table"><span id="S8.tab2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\TABLE</span>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<p id="S8.tab2.2" class="ltx_p">Summary of Manipulation Effects on Fixation, Knowledge Partitioning, and Overall Performance on LLMs
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">

<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;"><span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Manipulation</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fixation</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Knowledge Partitioning</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overall Idea Diversity</span></span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;">Human Seeding</span>
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">No meaningful effect</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">No meaningful effect</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">No meaningful effect</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;">Personas: Creative Entrepreneurs</span>
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.15pt;padding-bottom:1.15pt;">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S8.tab2.2.1.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">No meaningful effect</span>
</span></span>
