<td id="Ax5.T1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">27</td>
<td id="Ax5.T1.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">193</td>
<td id="Ax5.T1.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">830</td></tr>
<tr id="Ax5.T1.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Ax5.T1.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">LLM Persona + CoT (sequential)</td>
<td id="Ax5.T1.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">27</td>
<td id="Ax5.T1.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">203</td>
<td id="Ax5.T1.1.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">830</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="Ax5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax5.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Bootstrapped analysis (Tables <a href="#Ax5.T2" title="Table EC.2 ‣ Appendix E: CoT with Sequential Idea Generation ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">EC.2</span></a> and <a href="#Ax5.T3" title="Table EC.3 ‣ Appendix E: CoT with Sequential Idea Generation ‣ Examining and Addressing Barriers to Diversity in LLM-Generated Ideas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">EC.3</span></a>) further supports these findings. For the default LLM, adding CoT yields statistically significant gains across all three diversity metrics.
Unique categories increase from <math id="Ax5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{default}}=18.45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>default</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>18.45</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{default}}=18.45</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.11</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="Ax5.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{CoT}}=19.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>19.40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{CoT}}=19.40</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.10</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>;
unique combinations rise from <math id="Ax5.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{default}}=39.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>default</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>39.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{default}}=39.15</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.32</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="Ax5.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{CoT}}=41.92" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>41.92</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{CoT}}=41.92</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.28" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.28</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.28</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>;
and pairwise distance increases from <math id="Ax5.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{default}}=2.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>default</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{default}}=2.04</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="Ax5.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{CoT}}=2.13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{CoT}}=2.13</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.00</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>.
When combined with personas, however, the effect of CoT is more limited.
Categories show a significant increase from <math id="Ax5.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona}}=24.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>persona</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>24.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona}}=24.02</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.13</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="Ax5.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona+CoT}}=25.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>cat</mtext><mtext>persona+CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>25.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{cat}}^{\text{persona+CoT}}=25.04</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.12</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>,
but changes in unique combinations (<math id="Ax5.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=56.97" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>persona</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>56.97</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona}}=56.97</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.51" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.51</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.51</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="Ax5.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona+CoT}}=57.64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>comb</mtext><mtext>persona+CoT</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>57.64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{comb}}^{\text{persona+CoT}}=57.64</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.54</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.54</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="Ax5.p9.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.370" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.370</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.370</annotation></semantics></math>)
and pairwise distance (<math id="Ax5.p9.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{persona}}=2.36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>persona</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.36</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{persona}}=2.36</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="Ax5.p9.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{persona+CoT}}=2.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mtext>persona+CoT</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{persona+CoT}}=2.35</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax5.p9.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SE=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SE=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="Ax5.p9.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.177" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.177</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.177</annotation></semantics></math>) are small and not statistically significant.</p>
</div>
